.TH STICK-NOTE 1 "{{date}}" "Stick Note {{version}}" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stick-note \- a personal whiteboard of sticky notes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stick-note
[\fIoption\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stick-note
opens Stick Note: one endless whiteboard on which you stick notes made of text,
links and pictures. Where you put a note is how you find it again.
.PP
The first run starts a small background server on 127.0.0.1 and opens the board in
its own window when Chrome, Chromium, Edge or Brave is installed, or in the default
browser otherwise. The server quits by itself a few minutes after the last window
has been closed. Nothing leaves your computer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-stop
Ask a running Stick Note to quit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-data\-dir
Print the folder where the notes are stored and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short help text and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/stick-note
Your notes (board.json), pictures and daily backups. The directory named by
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is used instead when that variable is set. Removing the package never deletes it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PORT
TCP port of the local server (default 4747).
.TP
.B STICK_NOTE_DATA
Store the notes in this folder instead.
.TP
.B STICK_NOTE_BROWSER
Path of the Chromium-based browser used for the app window.
.TP
.B STICK_NOTE_NO_OPEN
When set, print the address instead of opening a window.
.TP
.B STICK_NOTE_IDLE_MS
Milliseconds without an open window before the background server quits (default 300000).
.SH SEE ALSO
